==Battleground==
*4 [[Helmut Krabbe]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.
*1 [[THE SLOTH]] spawns as the boss after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 2~6 seconds<sup>60f~180f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[Le'Prude]] spawns after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.
*3 [[Bore Jr.|Bore Jrs]] spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 66.67~73.33 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
An interesting but straightforward stage once you know what you're doing. Typically, the strategy is to remove either THE SLOTH or Le'Prude as fast as possible, making the stage much easier, and then chip down the remaining enemy. Units like [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Ironcat]] can help rush down THE SLOTH, while your usual Le'Prude counters like [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]] and [[Talents|Talented]] [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]] can quickly whittle down the problematic pachyderm.

Alternatively, you could play this stage like an endurance stage and outlast all three Bore Jrs, although this tends to be much harder than the aforementioned strategy. Nonetheless, using cats like [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]] and [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] can help remove Bore Jr from the field without touching THE SLOTH or Le'Prude if you want a challenge or don't have Dom Cat's Talents.

